From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Do not force HDR on SDR outputs.

PROTON_ENABLE_HDR=1 sets DXVK_HDR=1. The color-management output code
already detects whether HDR is enabled, but display enumeration overrides
an SDR result when that environment variable is set. Saints Row's native
Vulkan renderer fails on NVIDIA with HDR disabled on the monitor, and
works after enabling it.

Keep the compositor-reported HDR state instead of treating the opt-in as
proof of support. Apply DXVK_NO_HDR before generating HDR EDID metadata,
so an explicit disable cannot leave the output advertising HDR metadata.

DXVK also needs dxgi-respect-output-hdr-state.patch: its GetDesc1 otherwise
reports HDR based solely on DXVK_HDR, including to DXVK-NVAPI.

This does not alter Vulkan surface formats or colorspace conversion, and
leaves the X11/gamescope opt-in unchanged.

Follow-up to the color-management implementation by Etaash Mathamsetty
<45927311+Etaash-mathamsetty@users.noreply.github.com>.

Bug: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/541

Manual validation needed after rebuilding:
- Native Wayland, PROTON_ENABLE_HDR=1, monitor HDR off: launch in SDR.
- Repeat with monitor HDR on: retain working HDR.
- Test separate SDR/HDR outputs and DXVK_NO_HDR=1.
---

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/display.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/display.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/display.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/display.c
@@ -382,6 +382,9 @@
     /* We don't have a direct way to get the work area in Wayland. */
     monitor.rc_work = monitor.rc_monitor;
     monitor.hdr_enabled = output->supports_hdr;
+    /* An HDR request cannot enable HDR on an SDR compositor output. */
+    if ((env = getenv("DXVK_NO_HDR")) && *env == '1')
+        monitor.hdr_enabled = FALSE;
 
     info->flags = MONITOR_INFO_HAS_PRIMARIES | MONITOR_INFO_HAS_PREFERRED_MODE
                   | MONITOR_INFO_HAS_PHYSICAL_DIMENSIONS | MONITOR_INFO_HAS_MONITOR_NAME;
@@ -412,13 +415,8 @@
         info->flags |= MONITOR_INFO_HAS_CTA861_EXT;
     }
 
-    if ((env = getenv("DXVK_HDR")) && *env == '1')
-        monitor.hdr_enabled = TRUE;
-    else if ((env = getenv("DXVK_NO_HDR")) && *env == '1')
-        monitor.hdr_enabled = FALSE;
-
-    TRACE("name=%s rc_monitor=rc_work=%s\n",
-          output->name, wine_dbgstr_rect(&monitor.rc_monitor));
+    TRACE("name=%s rc_monitor=rc_work=%s hdr_enabled=%u\n",
+          output->name, wine_dbgstr_rect(&monitor.rc_monitor), monitor.hdr_enabled);
 
     device_manager->add_monitor(&monitor, param);
     free(monitor.edid);
